<p>Israel said its military will take control of a broad &quot;security zone&quot; in southern Lebanon up to the Litani River, and Defence Minister Israel Katz indicated troops could stay there until what he called the Hezbollah threat is removed. The announcement marks a significant escalation on Israel&#x27;s northern front and raises the prospect of a long-term Israeli presence inside Lebanese territory. Israeli officials cast the move as a security measure linked to attacks from Hezbollah and the need to protect residents of northern Israel. Foreign governments warned that a wider occupation would violate Lebanese sovereignty, deepen regional instability, and further worsen conditions for civilians already displaced by the fighting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JoQKUjFHF5bdkX4mZhltUAlbm3B4_7rqMhlE24lKrujNS6Aw7wV5pplXv6hlCT2Ps_zNXqcsD1szyOCJa4ba5BTviqe-ZE_pb9HPXuKzAzEH1MM_lfycSFZ-WfnR_Oc5Yn5Wo6W78LnBJ8gOoHtdP-fUoSEs1-TW9GH5GVhCBziuW1bF7CYDQRq-ClZA80jERn5aFeTexjV658LzwsFuGitpvvKU-v5MWWhWEGzz3BEgCrz6eo9rW-n9cyxJfMx0dMqD-rKceW3neR5Ayw' alt='Smoke rises from the site of an Israeli airstrike in the southern Lebanese coastal city of Tyre on March 24.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Return blocked: Katz said displaced Lebanese residents could not return to homes south of the Litani River until security for northern Israeli residents is ensured.</li><li>Territory scale: Israeli officials said the area would extend to the Litani River, roughly 30 to 40 kilometers north of Israel&#x27;s border and covering close to a tenth of Lebanon&#x27;s territory.</li><li>Access control: Katz said Israeli forces would control the &quot;remaining bridges&quot; along with the zone itself, suggesting the plan includes holding key routes into the area.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israel&#x27;s government: Katz tied the military plan not only to battlefield security but also to pressure on Beirut, after previously warning that Lebanon could lose territory if its government failed to disarm Hezbollah. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-israel-occupy-southern-lebanon/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: Hezbollah said it would resist any Israeli occupation of southern Lebanon, signaling that the announcement is more likely to extend the fighting than end it. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-israel-occupy-southern-lebanon/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Humanitarian groups: Aid-focused reporting said the biggest risk to civilians is a prolonged emergency, with displacement dragging on and already strained shelter, health, and basic-service systems deteriorating further. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens-as-fighting-continues/a-76512884'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-israel-occupy-southern-lebanon/'>Israel to seize parts of southern Lebanon as Hezbollah vows to resist occupation</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636087-israel-occupy-southern-lebanon-minister/'>Israel to occupy southern Lebanon – defense minister</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347801/israels-military-occupy-swathe-southern-lebanon-amid-widening-war'>Israel’s military to occupy swathe of southern Lebanon amid widening war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/lebanon-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens-as-fighting-continues/a-76512884'>Lebanon&#x27;s humanitarian crisis worsens as fighting continues</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/24/world/middleeast/israel-southern-lebanon-defense-minister.html'>Israel Plans to Control Large Parts of Southern Lebanon, Defense Minister Says</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/25/canada-tells-israel-that-lebanons-sovereignty-must-not-be-violated'>Canada tells Israel that Lebanon’s sovereignty ‘must not be violated’</a> 